          "tz": 120
        },
        "subject": "LU-20770 dbg: disable socklnd zero-copy for 2.16 interop test",
        "message": "LU-20770 dbg: disable socklnd zero-copy for 2.16 interop test\n\nDebug-only: raise the default zc_min_payload above the maximum\npayload, which is what LU-12945 did on hypervisors until LU-19763\n(bf67df32127, landed 2026-01-28) removed that guard.  The\nlustre-master interop matrix against 2.15/2.16 servers passed on\nbuild 4695 (2026-01-15) and hangs on every bulk write from build\n4697 (2026-01-29) on, on VM clients; if this passes where the\nbaseline times out, the zero-copy send path on VMs is the trigger.\n\nTest-Parameters: fortestonly testlist=sanity-pfl env=ONLY=\"18 19e\",ONLY_REPEAT=10 serverversion=2.16\nTest-Parameters: fortestonly testlist=sanity-pfl env=ONLY=\"18 19e\",ONLY_REPEAT=10 serverversion=2.16\nSigned-off-by: Marc Vef <mvef@whamcloud.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:Fable-5.1 llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: I26c52c197dedfbc820943735d8cc55308ca6c67d\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
